      DESCRIBE
TTTML -- A MACHINE THAT LEARNS TIC-TAC-TOE BY PLAYING
ITSELF, THEN PLAYS YOU WITH WHAT IT LEARNED. IT COMES
TRAINED.

   PLAY 1       PLAY IT, YOU MOVING FIRST, AS X
   PLAY 2       PLAY IT, IT MOVING FIRST
   TRIAL N      N GAMES EACH SIDE AGAINST A RANDOM PLAYER:
                WON, LOST AND DRAWN, AS X THEN AS O
   TRAIN N      FORGET, AND LEARN AGAIN FROM N GAMES
   SHOW S       A BOARD OF 9 SQUARES, 1 X, ¯1 O, 0 EMPTY

THE SQUARES ARE NUMBERED 1 TO 9, ROW BY ROW. WHAT IT LEARNS
IS A VALUE FOR EACH POSITION IT HAS MET, KEYS AND VALS, A
POSITION AND ITS 7 ROTATIONS AND REFLECTIONS COUNTED AS ONE:
ABOUT 750 OF THEM, AND 12,000 BYTES.
      ⍝ What it knows: a value for each position it has met.
